    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309045/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """[Tuesday, June 20, 1916, I Tatti]
0-12.
Magda had been for 10 months running a hospital in Belgium.She was most interesting. Trench was a bore. She had seen a woman crucified at a door with her breasts cut off, a child with both hands clipped off, another child transfixed to a barn-door with huge knife, and a mother with a child dead in her arms, shot by the commanding officer (German) as his answer to spare her husband for the sake of the 4 children – “there will be only 3 now”. The woman was crazy and no one could get the child out of her arms. 
June 21-24 pages cut away"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 154 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

